From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:39:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] ci: add publishing workflows (images, PyPI, site) with
 configurable targets

- docker-build.yml: builds a tool's image from its own folder and Dockerfile (symlinks materialized in the build context), tags and labels with docker/metadata-action, pushes to IMAGE_REGISTRY/IMAGE_NAMESPACE (repository variables).
- release.yml: for each tool released by release-please, v<version> and latest images (api, federation-api, query-tool), configure-nb-release.yml (PyPI upload; PYPI_REPOSITORY_URL selects the index) and sites.yml. recipes publishes nothing beyond its GitHub Release.
- sites.yml: query-tool on Netlify, only when SITE_DEPLOY is true; also runnable by hand for a released version.
- Nightly images: a `nightly` job in the api, federation-api and query-tool workflows, on push to main after the tool's tests pass; the workflows' own path filters decide which images are built.
- images-validation.yml (temporary, migration validation): manual build and push of every image with a validation-<sha> tag.
